1	/*
2	 * StreamScoop Utility Lake
3	 * File: streamscoop_utility_lake/src/main.c
4	 *
5	 * A lightweight data-lake helper that ingests CSV/JSON streams,
6	 * validates, transforms, and stores them into an embedded SQLite DB
7	 * while optionally rendering a live TUI dashboard.
8	 *
9	 * Build (example):
10	 *   gcc -Wall -Wextra -pedantic -std=c11 -pthread \
11	 *       main.c -lsqlite3 -lcurl -lncurses -o streamscoop
12	 *
13	 * NOTE: This file contains the application entry point and a minimal
14	 * yet functional implementation of the event-bus and observer pattern
15	 * sporting four observers:
16	 *   1) validator   – cheap schema checker
17	 *   2) transformer – dumb demo transformation
18	 *   3) storage     – SQLite writer
19	 *   4) dashboard   – live stats via ncurses
20	 *
21	 * In a real project, each observer would live in its own TU; they are
22	 * collapsed here for brevity.
23	 */
